# The reader Document must preserve both audiences

Slice A uses `/lore/services-capture-dependencies`. Its source has six bibliography entries, two glossary terms, internal links, and two pinned excerpts.

Decode the source through `parseLorePage` in `apps/site/scripts/content-lib.ts`. Do not replace structured `sources` and `terms` with strings.

## Inputs and authority

- Authored Brain content owns prose, bibliography, and terms.
- `packages/code-snippets` owns excerpt resolution and token output.
- The content generator owns heading and paragraph ids, citations, backlinks, and generation identity.
- One typed page descriptor owns route metadata. It includes source path, status, canonical policy, title, description, discovery links, robots, social image, and dates.
- The browser receives the complete document in Flags or initial Model. No initial Command fetches its body.

## Required Document shape

The one hand-converted page needs:

- Paragraphs containing text, code spans, links, paragraph anchors, and inbound counts.
- Headings with stable ids.
- Lists containing those same inline values.
- CodeSnippet nodes with source provenance, ranges, highlighted lines, and token data.
- A bibliography generated from decoded source records.
- Source/change metadata and linked-from entries generated by the existing graph.

Home additionally needs prompts, copy controls, diagrams, and tables. The shared shell owns nav, callout, agent pointer, breadcrumbs, and footer.

The later codemod must represent audience-specific blocks explicitly. Agent `read.text` cannot recover HumanOnly content. A rendered HTML string cannot recover a structured document safely.

## Migration boundary

This note describes the target. The hand-written Foldkit Document and its parity proof are still required.

The current preparation helper decodes the generated manifest/catalog, validates their generation, reads real HTML metadata, and decodes the selected lore frontmatter. Those old-renderer artifacts are comparison evidence. They must not become the replacement page's sole body implementation.

The initial route ledger covers 124 generated page paths and both HTML and Markdown representations. It is incomplete until special routes, aliases, redirects, and outcome/error statuses are added. Source paths for derived pages need explicit provenance.

No `@foldkit/markdown` pin is added for slice A. The content lane can use the verified shape when its dependency receives approval.

## Migration proof

The migration packet keeps all 166 `.svx` sources. It makes no route change.
The source AST has five component pages and 50 pinned snippet references.

`pnpm content:migrate --dry-run` compares agent Markdown from two independent trees.
The old component renderer reads `.svx`. The new renderer folds the Foldkit Document.
Both use the existing component definitions and snippet resolver.

- 162 pages compile with zero source-body diffs.
- Two pages contain raw HTML figures inside `HumanOnly`.
- `layer-startups` contains five task-list items.
- `structure-effect-by-domain` contains a literal brace placeholder. The conservative expression guard rejects it for hand review.
- The source AST has no reference links, footnotes, or inline components.
- The tool reports every rejected construct with its source path and line.
- A blocked run writes no candidates. A successful run writes outside the Brain.
- Candidate publication preflights all existing files. Repeated runs preserve identical files and refuse different files.

The hand page is `services-capture-dependencies`. Its fixture lives under `apps/web/test/fixtures/content-migration/`.
The hand page has six bibliography entries, two terms, internal links, and two pinned excerpts.

The test builds its body from the fixture and resolves excerpts before rendering.
It retains the existing generator's route decorations as a separate comparison seam.
The complete Document renders to the old response: 16,427 bytes, also verified against live Markdown.
The HTML test renders the same Document with a `CodeBlock` override and resolved snippet tokens.
No production route imports this proof.

## Frontmatter decision

Pre-split YAML before the Foldkit parser. Keep the YAML object beside the Document.
`MigrationFrontmatter` derives nested fields from `loreFrontmatterSchema`. The existing bibliography Schema decodes each source.
The hand page also uses `parseLorePage` for its public metadata rules.

One island table supplies both attribute validation and the mapper vocabulary.
Literal colons in text need escaping because the directive parser also recognizes timestamps.
Fenced code stays unchanged. Attribute escaping uses entities, not JSON backslash escapes.
List spread hints remain beside the Document because Foldkit does not retain them.
These hints preserve tight and loose lists in agent Markdown.

`oxfmt.config.ts` preserves prose wrapping only for the hand-fixture Markdown files.
Oxfmt adds one blank line to each empty reference fence. Neither addition changes the resolved Document or agent response.

A property generates plain-Markdown trees and compares complete agent output.
Another property checks decoded island attributes.
Dropping the first attribute character makes that property fail on its first run.
The mutation is restored. The mapper and filesystem publication checks pass.

## Cutover conditions

Do not cut over while any page fails or any round-trip diff remains.
Hand-map the figures and task state. Review the literal brace placeholder without changing the quoted source claim.
Extend full-route parity from the hand page to every public response, including graph decorations and metadata.
Keep the current route ledger and public URLs.

The current packet keeps the Markdown package build-only in both apps.
Worker graph checks reject it alongside code-snippets and Shiki.
A future renderer can admit the AST and view runtime separately from the Vite parser.
That change needs its own bundle proof.

Structured YAML support upstream would remove the pre-split adapter.
An upstream parser option without directive recognition would also simplify plain-text colons.
Preserving list spread would remove the list hints.
No upstream pull request is published by this packet.

Brain tooling still reads `.svx`. Its filename checks and pi-notes readers remain unchanged.
Before deletion, update their accepted extensions, link resolution, document discovery, and graph checks together.
Keep one authoritative source during that cutover. Do not make `.svx` and `.md` separate editable copies.

Related: [reader-site plan](./foldkit-site.svx).
